      "note": "No native past/to system; used '<hour> ramaj rik'in <minutes>' (ramaj = hour, rik'in = with), :30 = 'rik'in nik'aj' (half). Vigesimal minute numerals (wolajuj 15, juk'al 20, juk'al lajuj 30, kak'al 40, kak'al lajuj 50). Omitted a minute noun to avoid committing to the 'ch'utik ramaj' spelling in duration.units. Everyday Kaqchikel speakers often switch to Spanish for clock times, so a native check is advisable. Specific doubts: (1) whether 'rik'in' (with) is the connector speakers use between hour and minutes; (2) whether a minute noun ('ch'uti ramaj') is required after the numeral; (3) whether vigesimal compounds (juk'al wolajuj = 35) are what speakers actually say rather than Spanish numerals."
